{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EseJeNSTSXvErHwppBFnFW","type":"tool_result","content":"2026-11-02 19:20\nv24.22.1\nPython 3.14.8\nREADME.md\naudit.json\ndashboard.html\ndashboard.mjs\nmatrix.config.json\nprompt-template.md\nrun-matrix.mjs\nrun-record.mjs\nrun-record.schema.json\nruns\nstart-dashboard.ps1\nstart-dashboard.sh\ntest","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1a5e6f5c-3967-4e9e-a458-94f8949fc080","uuid":"28b38d79-27ec-460b-afa7-f783c3880734","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:20:49.848Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"2026-11-02 19:20\nv24.22.1\nPython 3.14.8\nREADME.md\naudit.json\ndashboard.html\ndashboard.mjs\nmatrix.config.json\nprompt-template.md\nrun-matrix.mjs\nrun-record.mjs\nrun-record.schema.json\nruns\nstart-dashboard.ps1\nstart-dashboard.sh\ntest","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EseJeNSTSXvErHwppBFnFW","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015VUtNizobFu6g2hP6KW48N","type":"tool_result","content":"## Files in `dist/handoff/`\n\nThe page lists these entries. It says \"View all files,\" so the listing may be incomplete.\n\n- **`docs/`**: Documentation, including `docs/ASSETS.md`, the asset card.\n- **`game/`**: A template game with `index.html`, `game.js`, and `test.mjs`. Copy it to start your own game.\n- **`kits/`**: Readable 2D genre kits. Each kit has a `<id>.js` game, a `<id>.html` page that plays it, and a headless test. `kits/README.md` lists them.\n- **`modules/`**: Optional engine modules, each loaded after the agent edition.\n- **`src/assets/`**: An asset store of CC0-derived object and material sets with catalogs.\n- **`tools/`**: Node scripts. `check.mjs` plays a game in headless Chromium and reports errors and state. `filmstrip.mjs` records frames. `replay.mjs` replays a recorded session. `asset-find.mjs`, `asset-sheet.mjs`, and `asset-set.mjs` work with the asset library.\n- **`API.md`**: The main API card. Read it first.\n- **`API-INDEX.md`**: A one-line-per-name index of public engine names. Search it rather than reading it whole.\n- **`AI_GUIDE.md`**: Recipes by genre, frame order, heights, and recorded sessions.\n- **`README.md`**: The package overview and instructions.\n- **`index.html`**: The page that plays the package's game.\n- **`my-3d2dge.js`**: The full engine in one readable file with no dependencies.\n- **`my-3d2dge-agent.js`**: The smaller \"agent edition\" of the engine, with a shorter manual in its header.\n- **`package.json`**: Pins Playwright for the tools.\n\n## Starting a game\n\nThe README suggests this order:\n\n1. Read `API.md`.\n2. Start from a kit in `kits/` or from the template in `game/`, rather than an empty file.\n3. Search `API-INDEX.md` for specific names.\n4. Consult `AI_GUIDE.md` for recipes.\n5. Don't build a pause menu, settings, key rebinding, full screen, or loading screen. The engine provides them. Customize them through `new E.Game({ menu: { items, settings, controls, quit } })`, and put heavy setup in `game.start({ boot: { steps } })`.\n\n## Engine API\n\nThe page does not show the exact script tag markup. It does show these names:\n\n- **Global namespace `E`**: Entry point for the engine. Examples are `new E.Game()`, `E.addAssets(...)`, `E.MATERIALS`, and `E.session`.\n- **`window.ASSETS`**: Asset sets are loaded with a script and then passed to `E.addAssets(window.ASSETS['kenney-furniture'])`.\n- **`game.start()`, `game.stop()`, `game.dispose()`**: Start, pause, and end a game.\n- **`game.advance(seconds)`**: Runs fixed 1/120 s steps headlessly. `advance(1)` runs 120 updates.\n- **`game.input`**: `tap('jump')` presses an action for one step. `hold('right')` holds it, and `hold('right', false)` releases it.\n- **`game.debug`**: Your handle for tests, with `snapshot()` and `teleport(x, y, z)`.\n- **`r.shape('barrel', x, y, 0, { facing })`**: Draws a library object in every view.\n- **Headless mode**: `new E.Game()` runs in Node or with `{ headless: true }`, with no screen, sound, or DOM.\n\n## Commands from the README\n\n```\nnpm install                          # Playwright, for the tools (once)\nnpx playwright install chromium      # its browser (once)\nnode game/test.mjs                   # headless test of the game\nnode tools/check.mjs game/index.html # play in a browser: errors, screenshots, snapshot\nnode kits/test.mjs arcade            # headless kit test\nnode tools/check.mjs kits/arcade.html#arcade/maze\nnode tools/filmstrip.mjs game/index.html --steps \"wait:800 press:Enter wait:500 rec:16:2 down:KeyD wait:600\" --seed 1\n```\n\nTo play, open `game/index.html` in a browser or serve the folder with `npx serve`. To share a single file, inline the two scripts into the page."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1a5e6f5c-3967-4e9e-a458-94f8949fc080","uuid":"2892c9d6-5367-4eae-a75d-7ce60fdaf85f","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:20:57.572Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":234271,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"## Files in `dist/handoff/`\n\nThe page lists these entries. It says \"View all files,\" so the listing may be incomplete.\n\n- **`docs/`**: Documentation, including `docs/ASSETS.md`, the asset card.\n- **`game/`**: A template game with `index.html`, `game.js`, and `test.mjs`. Copy it to start your own game.\n- **`kits/`**: Readable 2D genre kits. Each kit has a `<id>.js` game, a `<id>.html` page that plays it, and a headless test. `kits/README.md` lists them.\n- **`modules/`**: Optional engine modules, each loaded after the agent edition.\n- **`src/assets/`**: An asset store of CC0-derived object and material sets with catalogs.\n- **`tools/`**: Node scripts. `check.mjs` plays a game in headless Chromium and reports errors and state. `filmstrip.mjs` records frames. `replay.mjs` replays a recorded session. `asset-find.mjs`, `asset-sheet.mjs`, and `asset-set.mjs` work with the asset library.\n- **`API.md`**: The main API card. Read it first.\n- **`API-INDEX.md`**: A one-line-per-name index of public engine names. Search it rather than reading it whole.\n- **`AI_GUIDE.md`**: Recipes by genre, frame order, heights, and recorded sessions.\n- **`README.md`**: The package overview and instructions.\n- **`index.html`**: The page that plays the package's game.\n- **`my-3d2dge.js`**: The full engine in one readable file with no dependencies.\n- **`my-3d2dge-agent.js`**: The smaller \"agent edition\" of the engine, with a shorter manual in its header.\n- **`package.json`**: Pins Playwright for the tools.\n\n## Starting a game\n\nThe README suggests this order:\n\n1. Read `API.md`.\n2. Start from a kit in `kits/` or from the template in `game/`, rather than an empty file.\n3. Search `API-INDEX.md` for specific names.\n4. Consult `AI_GUIDE.md` for recipes.\n5. Don't build a pause menu, settings, key rebinding, full screen, or loading screen. The engine provides them. Customize them through `new E.Game({ menu: { items, settings, controls, quit } })`, and put heavy setup in `game.start({ boot: { steps } })`.\n\n## Engine API\n\nThe page does not show the exact script tag markup. It does show these names:\n\n- **Global namespace `E`**: Entry point for the engine. Examples are `new E.Game()`, `E.addAssets(...)`, `E.MATERIALS`, and `E.session`.\n- **`window.ASSETS`**: Asset sets are loaded with a script and then passed to `E.addAssets(window.ASSETS['kenney-furniture'])`.\n- **`game.start()`, `game.stop()`, `game.dispose()`**: Start, pause, and end a game.\n- **`game.advance(seconds)`**: Runs fixed 1/120 s steps headlessly. `advance(1)` runs 120 updates.\n- **`game.input`**: `tap('jump')` presses an action for one step. `hold('right')` holds it, and `hold('right', false)` releases it.\n- **`game.debug`**: Your handle for tests, with `snapshot()` and `teleport(x, y, z)`.\n- **`r.shape('barrel', x, y, 0, { facing })`**: Draws a library object in every view.\n- **Headless mode**: `new E.Game()` runs in Node or with `{ headless: true }`, with no screen, sound, or DOM.\n\n## Commands from the README\n\n```\nnpm install                          # Playwright, for the tools (once)\nnpx playwright install chromium      # its browser (once)\nnode game/test.mjs                   # headless test of the game\nnode tools/check.mjs game/index.html # play in a browser: errors, screenshots, snapshot\nnode kits/test.mjs arcade            # headless kit test\nnode tools/check.mjs kits/arcade.html#arcade/maze\nnode tools/filmstrip.mjs game/index.html --steps \"wait:800 press:Enter wait:500 rec:16:2 down:KeyD wait:600\" --seed 1\n```\n\nTo play, open `game/index.html` in a browser or serve the folder with `npx serve`. To share a single file, inline the two scripts into the page.","durationMs":8894,"url":"https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/tree/main/dist/handoff"},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_015VUtNizobFu6g2hP6KW48N","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UiJG28hA34t8AhTaCAChgN","type":"tool_result","content":"## Files in `lib/hub`\n\nThe page's directory listing shows:\n\n- `examples/` (folder)\n- `README.md`: the protocol spec\n- `bridge.js`\n- `harness.html`: the test harness\n- `retrofit.md`\n- `round.js`\n- `session.js`: the client\n\nThe listing is truncated (\"View all files\"), so there may be more.\n\n## Required files\n\n- **`session.js`** is pasted unmodified as the first script in the game's `<head>`, right after `<meta charset>`. The hub replaces unmodified copies with new versions, but not edited ones.\n- **The game page** (for example `GAME.html`) must carry the `hub:session` tags.\n- **Test files:** `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` are fetched next to the game to run the test.\n\n## Connecting\n\nThe game calls `AIHub.connect({ mode, seats: [min, max] })`, which returns a promise of `info` or `null`. `null` means no hub, so the game runs standalone. `AIHub.active` is `true` from the first line when a hub opened the page.\n\n`info` contains:\n\n- `me`: this copy's player id\n- `players`: `[{ id, name, color }]`, ids `0..N-1`\n- `host` and `isHost`\n- `server`: `true` for a host-only copy of a shared world\n- `mode`, `round`, `limitMs`\n- `seed`: shared by every copy, used by `AIHub.rng(label)`\n\nThen the game calls `AIHub.ready()` once. The round starts on the hub's clock, and `AIHub.time()` reads the shared timeline.\n\n## Functions\n\n| Call | Used in |\n|---|---|\n| `connect({ mode, seats })` | all |\n| `ready()` | all |\n| `time()` | all |\n| `on(event, fn)` | all; returns an unsubscribe function |\n| `progress({ score, label })` | parallel, ghost |\n| `result({ time \\| score, stats?, awards? })` | parallel, ghost; once |\n| `finish({ standings, scores?, won?, stats?, awards? })` | shared world; host only, once |\n| `send(data, { to, reliable })` | ghost, shared world; returns `false` if dropped |\n| `rng(label)` | all; numbers in `[0, 1)` |\n| `fail(message)` | all |\n\n`seeded` reports whether the client seeded `Math.random`.\n\n## Events\n\n- `start`: `{ in }`, milliseconds until play begins\n- `message`: `(data, from)`\n- `leave`: `{ id, reason }`, where reason is `left`, `disconnected`, `not-ready` or `kicked`\n- `time-up`: `{ graceMs }`\n- `end`: `{ reason, standings }`, where reason is `finished`, `void`, `host-left`, `sat-out` or `session-ended`\n\n## Messages\n\n- `send()` payloads are JSON, at most 16 KB.\n- Each copy may send about 20 messages per second, with bursts up to 40. Extra messages are dropped.\n- Reliable messages (the default) arrive in order. Unreliable ones may be lost or reordered, and any unreliable message over about 1,200 bytes is lost whole if one packet is lost.\n\n## Catalogue and tags\n\nThe hub tests each game when it joins the library and drops games that fail. The page's `<head>` tags are:\n\n- `hub:session`: `1`\n- `hub:session-players`: `MIN-MAX`\n- `hub:session-mode`: `parallel`, `ghost` or `shared-world`\n- `hub:session-goal` and `hub:session-howto`: shown on the hub's card\n\nOptional tags are `hub:session-minutes` and `hub:webgpu` (set to `required`).\n\nThe page doesn't define a separate run-record format. The closest equivalents are the tags and the harness's pass flag, `window.__hubCheck.pass`, which must be `true`.\n\n## URLs\n\n- Spec: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md`\n- Client: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js`\n- Harness: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html`\n\nLocal test: serve the folder with `python3 -m http.server 8000` and open `harness.html?game=GAME.html&players=2&auto=1`."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1a5e6f5c-3967-4e9e-a458-94f8949fc080","uuid":"b8d84175-7b66-431a-978b-5ec7a5ee283a","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:20:59.407Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":287997,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"## Files in `lib/hub`\n\nThe page's directory listing shows:\n\n- `examples/` (folder)\n- `README.md`: the protocol spec\n- `bridge.js`\n- `harness.html`: the test harness\n- `retrofit.md`\n- `round.js`\n- `session.js`: the client\n\nThe listing is truncated (\"View all files\"), so there may be more.\n\n## Required files\n\n- **`session.js`** is pasted unmodified as the first script in the game's `<head>`, right after `<meta charset>`. The hub replaces unmodified copies with new versions, but not edited ones.\n- **The game page** (for example `GAME.html`) must carry the `hub:session` tags.\n- **Test files:** `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` are fetched next to the game to run the test.\n\n## Connecting\n\nThe game calls `AIHub.connect({ mode, seats: [min, max] })`, which returns a promise of `info` or `null`. `null` means no hub, so the game runs standalone. `AIHub.active` is `true` from the first line when a hub opened the page.\n\n`info` contains:\n\n- `me`: this copy's player id\n- `players`: `[{ id, name, color }]`, ids `0..N-1`\n- `host` and `isHost`\n- `server`: `true` for a host-only copy of a shared world\n- `mode`, `round`, `limitMs`\n- `seed`: shared by every copy, used by `AIHub.rng(label)`\n\nThen the game calls `AIHub.ready()` once. The round starts on the hub's clock, and `AIHub.time()` reads the shared timeline.\n\n## Functions\n\n| Call | Used in |\n|---|---|\n| `connect({ mode, seats })` | all |\n| `ready()` | all |\n| `time()` | all |\n| `on(event, fn)` | all; returns an unsubscribe function |\n| `progress({ score, label })` | parallel, ghost |\n| `result({ time \\| score, stats?, awards? })` | parallel, ghost; once |\n| `finish({ standings, scores?, won?, stats?, awards? })` | shared world; host only, once |\n| `send(data, { to, reliable })` | ghost, shared world; returns `false` if dropped |\n| `rng(label)` | all; numbers in `[0, 1)` |\n| `fail(message)` | all |\n\n`seeded` reports whether the client seeded `Math.random`.\n\n## Events\n\n- `start`: `{ in }`, milliseconds until play begins\n- `message`: `(data, from)`\n- `leave`: `{ id, reason }`, where reason is `left`, `disconnected`, `not-ready` or `kicked`\n- `time-up`: `{ graceMs }`\n- `end`: `{ reason, standings }`, where reason is `finished`, `void`, `host-left`, `sat-out` or `session-ended`\n\n## Messages\n\n- `send()` payloads are JSON, at most 16 KB.\n- Each copy may send about 20 messages per second, with bursts up to 40. Extra messages are dropped.\n- Reliable messages (the default) arrive in order. Unreliable ones may be lost or reordered, and any unreliable message over about 1,200 bytes is lost whole if one packet is lost.\n\n## Catalogue and tags\n\nThe hub tests each game when it joins the library and drops games that fail. The page's `<head>` tags are:\n\n- `hub:session`: `1`\n- `hub:session-players`: `MIN-MAX`\n- `hub:session-mode`: `parallel`, `ghost` or `shared-world`\n- `hub:session-goal` and `hub:session-howto`: shown on the hub's card\n\nOptional tags are `hub:session-minutes` and `hub:webgpu` (set to `required`).\n\nThe page doesn't define a separate run-record format. The closest equivalents are the tags and the harness's pass flag, `window.__hubCheck.pass`, which must be `true`.\n\n## URLs\n\n- Spec: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md`\n- Client: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js`\n- Harness: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html`\n\nLocal test: serve the folder with `python3 -m http.server 8000` and open `harness.html?game=GAME.html&players=2&auto=1`.","durationMs":10015,"url":"https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub"},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UiJG28hA34t8AhTaCAChgN","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
