{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qj26m6bv8a7p9e2XFdmHa6","type":"tool_result","content":"ok game/index.html 1397\nok game/game.js 9122\nok game/test.mjs 2609\nok kits/README.md 6980\n/*!\n * my-3D2dge v0.85.1  (My \"3D\" 2D Game Engine)\n * Procedural pixel-puppet engine for every 2D perspective.\n * https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge  (MIT License)\n *\n * READ THIS FIRST (humans and AI models extending a my-3D2dge game)\n * -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n * 0. EVERY GAME STARTS WITH  const E = My3D2dge;  and then uses E.Game, E.px, ...\n * 1. WORLD SPACE IS 3D. x = east, y = south, z = up. One floor tile = 16 units.\n *    Game logic never thinks about screen pixels.\n * 2. A VIEW turns world points into screen pixels. Swap the view and the whole game\n *    re-renders from another angle: E.VIEWS.iso, .threequarter, .topdown,\n *    .brawler, .side  (or build your own: new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale, zBoost)).\n * 3. CHARACTERS ARE RIGS, NOT SPRITES. E.Humanoid and E.Blob recompute their\n *    joints from math every step, in 3D, then project them. That is why they move\n *    fluidly and can face any angle in any view without extra art. Small things\n *    (coins, bullets, icons) can be pixel sprites written as strings: E.sprite().\n * 4. PIXEL RULES. Draw with E.px (rect, line, disc, ell, poly, sprite...). Every shape\n *    snaps to whole pixels. Never use ctx.arc / ctx.stroke / ctx.fillText on the game\n *    buffer: they anti-alias and break the look. Translucency and glow go through\n *    px.blend / polyDither / ddisc / r.glowDisc: stepped alpha and blend modes like PS1\n *    hardware (E.style.trans = '\n7:## North star\n17:## The mental model\n29:## Remake workflow (port, remaster, reimagine, remix)\n44:## Visual craft: aim for PS1 / N64 era 2D, not NES\n64:## Animation: fluid, varied, readable\n72:## Hard rules\n82:## Standard features (built in: adjust them, don't rebuild them)\n120:## Frame order\n140:## Systems in more depth\n142:### Views and resolution\n150:### Scenes\n155:### Camera\n163:### Players (two to four on one machine)\n169:### Motion and timing (tweens, scripts, paths)\n178:### TileMap (ground-plane levels)\n190:### Heights: roofs, ledges, sight and reach\n222:### PlatformMap (side-scrolling levels)\n242:### Platformer (side-scroller controller)\n249:### Body (ground-plane physics)\n255:### Mover and actions (third-person ground controller)\n267:### Perception (sight, hearing, suspicion)\n273:### Attack (melee timing)\n280:### Bullets and patterns\n286:### Humanoid\n297:### Audio\n305:### Text and UI\n311:### Shell (an HTML interface: screens and HUD)\n319:### Lighting\n328:### Errors and warnings\n338:### Testing without a browser\n357:### The handoff package\n360:### Modules (general systems in files of their own)\n367:### Kits and the diet (which file for which game)\n374:### Recorded sessions (a bug from a phone, replayed exactly)\n402:## Genre recipes\n606:## Building a big game: lessons from Emberdeep\n631:## Where to find more: animation and examples\n648:## Performance\n656:## Checklist before handing a game back\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium__20261102-192041__x694301/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1a5e6f5c-3967-4e9e-a458-94f8949fc080","uuid":"e043154c-d0e4-46c7-b4a8-f207826a06c3","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:21:36.213Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"ok game/index.html 1397\nok game/game.js 9122\nok game/test.mjs 2609\nok kits/README.md 6980\n/*!\n * my-3D2dge v0.85.1  (My \"3D\" 2D Game Engine)\n * Procedural pixel-puppet engine for every 2D perspective.\n * https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge  (MIT License)\n *\n * READ THIS FIRST (humans and AI models extending a my-3D2dge game)\n * -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n * 0. EVERY GAME STARTS WITH  const E = My3D2dge;  and then uses E.Game, E.px, ...\n * 1. WORLD SPACE IS 3D. x = east, y = south, z = up. One floor tile = 16 units.\n *    Game logic never thinks about screen pixels.\n * 2. A VIEW turns world points into screen pixels. Swap the view and the whole game\n *    re-renders from another angle: E.VIEWS.iso, .threequarter, .topdown,\n *    .brawler, .side  (or build your own: new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale, zBoost)).\n * 3. CHARACTERS ARE RIGS, NOT SPRITES. E.Humanoid and E.Blob recompute their\n *    joints from math every step, in 3D, then project them. That is why they move\n *    fluidly and can face any angle in any view without extra art. Small things\n *    (coins, bullets, icons) can be pixel sprites written as strings: E.sprite().\n * 4. PIXEL RULES. Draw with E.px (rect, line, disc, ell, poly, sprite...). Every shape\n *    snaps to whole pixels. Never use ctx.arc / ctx.stroke / ctx.fillText on the game\n *    buffer: they anti-alias and break the look. Translucency and glow go through\n *    px.blend / polyDither / ddisc / r.glowDisc: stepped alpha and blend modes like PS1\n *    hardware (E.style.trans = '\n7:## North star\n17:## The mental model\n29:## Remake workflow (port, remaster, reimagine, remix)\n44:## Visual craft: aim for PS1 / N64 era 2D, not NES\n64:## Animation: fluid, varied, readable\n72:## Hard rules\n82:## Standard features (built in: adjust them, don't rebuild them)\n120:## Frame order\n140:## Systems in more depth\n142:### Views and resolution\n150:### Scenes\n155:### Camera\n163:### Players (two to four on one machine)\n169:### Motion and timing (tweens, scripts, paths)\n178:### TileMap (ground-plane levels)\n190:### Heights: roofs, ledges, sight and reach\n222:### PlatformMap (side-scrolling levels)\n242:### Platformer (side-scroller controller)\n249:### Body (ground-plane physics)\n255:### Mover and actions (third-person ground controller)\n267:### Perception (sight, hearing, suspicion)\n273:### Attack (melee timing)\n280:### Bullets and patterns\n286:### Humanoid\n297:### Audio\n305:### Text and UI\n311:### Shell (an HTML interface: screens and HUD)\n319:### Lighting\n328:### Errors and warnings\n338:### Testing without a browser\n357:### The handoff package\n360:### Modules (general systems in files of their own)\n367:### Kits and the diet (which file for which game)\n374:### Recorded sessions (a bug from a phone, replayed exactly)\n402:## Genre recipes\n606:## Building a big game: lessons from Emberdeep\n631:## Where to find more: animation and examples\n648:## Performance\n656:## Checklist before handing a game back","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium__20261102-192041__x694301/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Qj26m6bv8a7p9e2XFdmHa6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgfCNeSs8csxjV47zvgH9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01386X5GTeASzLX7cxZA7ivu","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/ref-engine && cat game/index.html && cat game/game.js","description":"Read the template game page and script"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5452,"cache_read_input_tokens":64584,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5452,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1a5e6f5c-3967-4e9e-a458-94f8949fc080","uuid":"db5d785a-c484-4205-9b85-205911e69b90","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:21:37.117Z","request_id":"req_011CgfCNe5nnHPVNgLyfY623","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01386X5GTeASzLX7cxZA7ivu":{"command":"cd /tmp/ref-engine && cat game/index.html && cat game/game.js","description":"Read the template game page and script"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01386X5GTeASzLX7cxZA7ivu","type":"tool_result","content":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n<title>Rooftop · my-3D2dge template</title>\n<style>html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #000; overflow: hidden } #screen { width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; image-rendering: pixelated; touch-action: none }</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div id=\"e3-boot\" role=\"status\" style=\"position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:40;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:flex-end;gap:6px;padding:20px;background:#05040a;color:#a9a1c8;font:12px/1.5 ui-monospace,Menlo,Consolas,monospace\"><style>@keyframes e3-run{from{transform:translateX(-100%)}to{transform:translateX(340%)}}@keyframes e3-late{to{opacity:1}}</style><b style=\"color:#f4f0ff;font-size:16px;letter-spacing:.08em\">ROOFTOP</b><span>Starting · my-3D2dge v0.85.1</span><span style=\"display:block;height:4px;max-width:440px;overflow:hidden;background:#ffffff14\"><span style=\"display:block;width:30%;height:100%;background:#d9b77c;animation:e3-run 1.2s ease-in-out infinite\"></span></span><span style=\"opacity:0;animation:e3-late .3s 12s forwards\">Still starting. If this stays, the game's script did not run: reload, or open the browser's console.</span></div>\n<canvas id=\"screen\"></canvas>\n<script src=\"../my-3d2dge.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"game.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n// The handoff package's template game: a rooftop thief in the isometric view. Climb onto the roof, take the gem, and\n// don't let the guard in the street watch you for long. It shows what a game is made of (scenes, a TileMap with roofs, a\n// Mover and a Humanoid, input, the camera, a HUD) and the height-aware API: E.Mover climbs any wall (climbAny: jump at\n// it, the stick climbs, jump leaps up, it pulls up at the top) and glides (glide: jump again in the air; a sail drawn\n// over it), both on its stamina, the guard is a plain Body, map.sight and E.inArc for\n// the guard's eyes (they see over the planter, not through the roof), shapes and materials (docs/ASSETS.md: barrels and\n// crates as data, solid with map.solid; the street's cobbles a material), and game.debug for tests and tools. The pause menu,\n// settings, rebinding and full screen come with every game: menu: { controls } names the actions on its Controls screen,\n// and input.label() puts the player's own key or button in a prompt. The night is canvas lighting (game.lights): an\n// ambient, and lights added every draw (a street lamp, the gem's glow), the same in every browser and every check. The\n// HUD is HTML (E.Shell: the objective with its distance, the guard's alert, your keys), over the pixels; the title and\n// end screens are pixel art.\n// Copy it and make it your game. Test it headless: node game/test.mjs. Check it in a browser: node tools/check.mjs game/index.html\n(() => {\nconst E = My3D2dge;\nconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'snes', expand: true, view: 'iso', views: ['iso', 'threequarter'],   // expand: full screen at any shape (the HUD anchors to r.W, r.H)\n  menu: { controls: { jump: 'Jump and climb', attack: false, dash: false, skill: false } } });   // (this game uses moves and jump only)\nconst ui = new E.Shell(game);   // the HTML HUD (it keeps the standard pause menu); headless, it draws nothing\nconst ROOF = 32;\nconst map = new E.TileMap({\n  rows: ['############',\n         '#..........#',\n         '#.@........#',\n         '#....p.....#',\n         '#......RRR.#',\n         '#......RGR.#',\n         '#..s...RRR.#',\n         '#..........#',\n         '############'],\n  legend: { '#': 1, R: 2, G: { tile: 2, spawn: 'gem' }, p: 3, '@': 'hero', s: 'guard' },\n  types: { 1: { h: 48, top: '#5a5068', side: '#3e3650', cut: true },\n           2: { h: ROOF, top: '#9a4a3a', side: '#c8b89a', face: 'plaster', roof: 'tiles' },\n           3: { h: 10, top: '#3e7a3a', side: '#5a4a32', face: 'plank', roof: 'leaves' } },\n  floorMat: 'cobble'   // a material (E.MATERIALS, or '#hex pattern'): the floor, wall faces and tops, shapes' parts all take them\n});\n// set dressing: shapes (E.SHAPES: objects as data, right in every view), solid where they stand (map.solid: walk into one, land on it)\nconst DRESS = [['barrel', 152, 30, { facing: .5 }], ['barrel', 166, 26, { facing: 2 }], ['crate', 22, 120, { facing: .3 }], ['cart', 72, 26, { facing: 0 }]];\nfor (const [id, x, y, o] of DRESS) map.solid(id, x, y, 0, o);\nconst GEM = E.sprite(['.c.', 'cCc', '.c.'], { c: '#48c8f0', C: '#e8faff' }, 2);\nlet hero, heroRig, guard, guardRig, alert, got, won;\n\nfunction reset() {\n  const h = map.find('hero'), g = map.find('guard');\n  hero = new E.Mover({ x: h.x, y: h.y, r: 5, climbAny: true, climbMax: 24, glide: true, staminaMax: 100 }); hero.facing = 0;   // (the roof, 32 high, is climbed)\n  heroRig = heroRig || new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.2, build: 'heroic', weapon: null, hood: true, outfit: 'coat', colors: { cloth: '#3a4a6a', cape: '#2a3a52' } });\n  guard = new E.Body({ x: g.x, y: g.y, r: 5 }); guard.facing = 0; guard.dir = 1;\n  guardRig = guardRig || new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.2, build: 'heroic', weapon: 'sword', hat: 'helmet', colors: { cloth: '#8a3a32' } });\n  alert = 0; got = false; won = false;\n}\n\nconst title = {\n  update() { if (game.input.pressed('start')) { reset(); game.go('play'); } },\n  draw(r) {\n    r.sky(['#141030', '#3a2a60']);\n    const m = Math.round(r.H / 2);   // centred on any screen\n    r.overlay(g => E.font.title(g, 'ROOFTOP', r.W / 2, m - 52, { scale: 3, align: 'center' }));\n    r.text(('CLIMB WITH ' + game.input.label('jump') + '  TAKE THE GEM  STAY UNSEEN').toUpperCase(), r.W / 2, m + 8, '#e8e0ff', { align: 'center' });\n    r.text(('PRESS ' + game.input.label('start')).toUpperCase(), r.W / 2, m + 38, '#ffffff', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000' });\n  }\n};\n\nconst play = {\n  pausable: true,\n  enter() { game.follow(hero, { z: 16 }); game.cam.bounds = v => map.bounds(v); game.lights.enabled = true; game.lights.ambient = .5; },\n  exit() { game.lights.enabled = false; ui.hud({}); },\n  update(dt) {\n    const I = game.input, was = !!(hero.wall || hero.action);\n    hero.update(dt, map, I);   // walks, jumps, climbs: the stick and the jump button, through the view\n    if (!was && (hero.wall || hero.action)) game.audio.sfx('jump');\n    // the guard walks the street and watches ahead: its eyes see over the planter, not through the roof\n    guard.vx = guard.dir * 30; guard.update(dt, map);\n    if (guard.x > 112 || guard.hitWall) guard.dir = -1; else if (guard.x < 40) guard.dir = 1;\n    guard.facing = guard.dir > 0 ? 0 : Math.PI;\n    const sees = map.sight(guard, hero) && E.inArc(guard, guard.facing, hero, 110, .6);\n    alert = sees ? alert + dt : Math.max(0, alert - dt * .5);\n    const gem = map.find('gem');\n    if (!got && E.dist(hero, { x: gem.x, y: gem.y, z: ROOF }) < 12) { got = true; game.audio.sfx('coin'); game.flash('#c8f4ff', .15); }\n    if (got && hero.z < 2) { won = true; game.go('end'); }   // back down in the street with it\n    else if (alert > 1.2) { won = false; game.audio.sfx('hurt'); game.go('end'); }\n    // the rigs are posed every step from the bodies' motion; draw only draws them\n    heroRig.update(dt, hero.rigState());\n    guardRig.update(dt, { x: guard.x, y: guard.y, z: guard.z, vx: guard.vx, vy: 0, facing: guard.facing, stance: 'ready' });\n    // the HUD, from this step's state (E.Shell redraws only what changed; the keys hide on a touch screen)\n    ui.hud({ objective: got ? { title: 'Bring it down', text: 'Back to the street with it' } : { title: 'Take the gem', text: hero.wall ? 'Climb: up, and jump to leap' : 'It lies on the roof', at: { x: gem.x, y: gem.y, z: ROOF }, from: hero },\n      bars: [{ label: 'Seen', value: Math.min(alert, 1.2), max: 1.2, color: '#ff6040' }, { label: 'Stamina', value: hero.stamina, max: hero.staminaMax, color: hero.exhausted ? '#ff6040' : '#7ad06a' }],\n      keys: [[['up', 'left', 'down', 'right'].map(a => I.label(a)).join(''), 'Move'], [I.label('jump'), 'Jump, climb, glide']] });\n  },\n  draw(r) {\n    map.drawFloor(r); map.queueWalls(r);   // (the floor runs on past the map to the screen's edges: map.outside)\n    for (const [id, x, y, o] of DRESS) r.shape(id, x, y, 0, o);\n    r.prop('lamp', 88, 88, 0, { light: true });   // a street lamp: its glow and a pool of light\n    r.decal(() => r.groundArc(guard.x, guard.y, 6, 110, guard.facing - .6, guard.facing + .6, alert > 0 ? '#ff6040' : '#ffe080', .4));   // its sight cone\n    const gem = map.find('gem');\n    if (!got) { r.sprite(gem.x, gem.y, ROOF + 6 + Math.sin(game.time * 3) * 2, GEM, { glow: .8 }); game.lights.add(gem.x, gem.y, ROOF + 6, 44, .9, { color: '#80d8ff' }); }\n    if (hero.gliding) r.queue(hero.x, hero.y, hero.z + 40, g => {   // the sail, over the hands the rig holds up\n      const c = Math.cos(hero.facing), s = Math.sin(hero.facing), P = (f, w, z) => r.w(hero.x + c * f - s * w, hero.y + s * f + c * w, hero.z + z);\n      const q = [P(9, -17, 43), P(9, 17, 43), P(-7, 15, 37), P(-7, -15, 37)], h = P(0, 0, 30);\n      for (const t of [q[0], q[1]]) E.px.line(g, t[0], t[1], h[0], h[1], '#3a2a20');\n      E.px.poly(g, q, '#d8603a'); E.px.line(g, q[0][0], q[0][1], q[1][0], q[1][1], '#f4a070');\n    });\n    for (const [b, rig] of [[hero, heroRig], [guard, guardRig]]) {\n      r.shadow(b.x, b.y, 7, .35, undefined, b.groundZ || 0);\n      r.actor(b.x, b.y, b.z, (g, ox, oy) => rig.draw(g, ox, oy, r.view));\n    }\n  }\n};\n\nconst end = {\n  update() { if (game.input.pressed('start')) { reset(); game.go('play'); } },\n  draw(r) {\n    r.sky(won ? ['#103020', '#2a6a48'] : ['#301010', '#6a2a2a']);\n    const m = Math.round(r.H / 2);\n    r.overlay(g => E.font.title(g, won ? 'STOLEN' : 'CAUGHT', r.W / 2, m - 42, { scale: 3, align: 'center' }));\n    r.text(('PRESS ' + game.input.label('start') + ' TO TRY AGAIN').toUpperCase(), r.W / 2, m + 28, '#ffffff', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000' });\n  }\n};\n\nreset();\n// a handle for tests and tools (node game/test.mjs, tools/check.mjs prints snapshot(), tools/replay.mjs logs it)\ngame.debug = {\n  snapshot: () => ({ scene: game.sceneName, hero: [hero.x, hero.y, hero.z].map(v => Math.round(v * 10) / 10), climbing: !!(hero.wall || hero.action),\n    guard: [Math.round(guard.x), Math.round(guard.y), guard.facing], alert: Math.round(alert * 100) / 100, got, won }),\n  teleport(x, y, z = 0, facing = hero.facing) { Object.assign(hero, { x, y, z, vx: 0, vy: 0, vz: 0, onGround: true, facing, wall: null, action: null }); }\n};\ngame.start({ scenes: { title, play, end }, scene: 'title' });\n})();\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium__20261102-192041__x694301/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1a5e6f5c-3967-4e9e-a458-94f8949fc080","uuid":"700cdaab-4237-4266-9078-e0fae33e796c","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:21:37.137Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n<title>Rooftop · my-3D2dge template</title>\n<style>html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #000; overflow: hidden } #screen { width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; image-rendering: pixelated; touch-action: none }</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div id=\"e3-boot\" role=\"status\" style=\"position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:40;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:flex-end;gap:6px;padding:20px;background:#05040a;color:#a9a1c8;font:12px/1.5 ui-monospace,Menlo,Consolas,monospace\"><style>@keyframes e3-run{from{transform:translateX(-100%)}to{transform:translateX(340%)}}@keyframes e3-late{to{opacity:1}}</style><b style=\"color:#f4f0ff;font-size:16px;letter-spacing:.08em\">ROOFTOP</b><span>Starting · my-3D2dge v0.85.1</span><span style=\"display:block;height:4px;max-width:440px;overflow:hidden;background:#ffffff14\"><span style=\"display:block;width:30%;height:100%;background:#d9b77c;animation:e3-run 1.2s ease-in-out infinite\"></span></span><span style=\"opacity:0;animation:e3-late .3s 12s forwards\">Still starting. If this stays, the game's script did not run: reload, or open the browser's console.</span></div>\n<canvas id=\"screen\"></canvas>\n<script src=\"../my-3d2dge.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"game.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n// The handoff package's template game: a rooftop thief in the isometric view. Climb onto the roof, take the gem, and\n// don't let the guard in the street watch you for long. It shows what a game is made of (scenes, a TileMap with roofs, a\n// Mover and a Humanoid, input, the camera, a HUD) and the height-aware API: E.Mover climbs any wall (climbAny: jump at\n// it, the stick climbs, jump leaps up, it pulls up at the top) and glides (glide: jump again in the air; a sail drawn\n// over it), both on its stamina, the guard is a plain Body, map.sight and E.inArc for\n// the guard's eyes (they see over the planter, not through the roof), shapes and materials (docs/ASSETS.md: barrels and\n// crates as data, solid with map.solid; the street's cobbles a material), and game.debug for tests and tools. The pause menu,\n// settings, rebinding and full screen come with every game: menu: { controls } names the actions on its Controls screen,\n// and input.label() puts the player's own key or button in a prompt. The night is canvas lighting (game.lights): an\n// ambient, and lights added every draw (a street lamp, the gem's glow), the same in every browser and every check. The\n// HUD is HTML (E.Shell: the objective with its distance, the guard's alert, your keys), over the pixels; the title and\n// end screens are pixel art.\n// Copy it and make it your game. Test it headless: node game/test.mjs. Check it in a browser: node tools/check.mjs game/index.html\n(() => {\nconst E = My3D2dge;\nconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'snes', expand: true, view: 'iso', views: ['iso', 'threequarter'],   // expand: full screen at any shape (the HUD anchors to r.W, r.H)\n  menu: { controls: { jump: 'Jump and climb', attack: false, dash: false, skill: false } } });   // (this game uses moves and jump only)\nconst ui = new E.Shell(game);   // the HTML HUD (it keeps the standard pause menu); headless, it draws nothing\nconst ROOF = 32;\nconst map = new E.TileMap({\n  rows: ['############',\n         '#..........#',\n         '#.@........#',\n         '#....p.....#',\n         '#......RRR.#',\n         '#......RGR.#',\n         '#..s...RRR.#',\n         '#..........#',\n         '############'],\n  legend: { '#': 1, R: 2, G: { tile: 2, spawn: 'gem' }, p: 3, '@': 'hero', s: 'guard' },\n  types: { 1: { h: 48, top: '#5a5068', side: '#3e3650', cut: true },\n           2: { h: ROOF, top: '#9a4a3a', side: '#c8b89a', face: 'plaster', roof: 'tiles' },\n           3: { h: 10, top: '#3e7a3a', side: '#5a4a32', face: 'plank', roof: 'leaves' } },\n  floorMat: 'cobble'   // a material (E.MATERIALS, or '#hex pattern'): the floor, wall faces and tops, shapes' parts all take them\n});\n// set dressing: shapes (E.SHAPES: objects as data, right in every view), solid where they stand (map.solid: walk into one, land on it)\nconst DRESS = [['barrel', 152, 30, { facing: .5 }], ['barrel', 166, 26, { facing: 2 }], ['crate', 22, 120, { facing: .3 }], ['cart', 72, 26, { facing: 0 }]];\nfor (const [id, x, y, o] of DRESS) map.solid(id, x, y, 0, o);\nconst GEM = E.sprite(['.c.', 'cCc', '.c.'], { c: '#48c8f0', C: '#e8faff' }, 2);\nlet hero, heroRig, guard, guardRig, alert, got, won;\n\nfunction reset() {\n  const h = map.find('hero'), g = map.find('guard');\n  hero = new E.Mover({ x: h.x, y: h.y, r: 5, climbAny: true, climbMax: 24, glide: true, staminaMax: 100 }); hero.facing = 0;   // (the roof, 32 high, is climbed)\n  heroRig = heroRig || new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.2, build: 'heroic', weapon: null, hood: true, outfit: 'coat', colors: { cloth: '#3a4a6a', cape: '#2a3a52' } });\n  guard = new E.Body({ x: g.x, y: g.y, r: 5 }); guard.facing = 0; guard.dir = 1;\n  guardRig = guardRig || new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.2, build: 'heroic', weapon: 'sword', hat: 'helmet', colors: { cloth: '#8a3a32' } });\n  alert = 0; got = false; won = false;\n}\n\nconst title = {\n  update() { if (game.input.pressed('start')) { reset(); game.go('play'); } },\n  draw(r) {\n    r.sky(['#141030', '#3a2a60']);\n    const m = Math.round(r.H / 2);   // centred on any screen\n    r.overlay(g => E.font.title(g, 'ROOFTOP', r.W / 2, m - 52, { scale: 3, align: 'center' }));\n    r.text(('CLIMB WITH ' + game.input.label('jump') + '  TAKE THE GEM  STAY UNSEEN').toUpperCase(), r.W / 2, m + 8, '#e8e0ff', { align: 'center' });\n    r.text(('PRESS ' + game.input.label('start')).toUpperCase(), r.W / 2, m + 38, '#ffffff', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000' });\n  }\n};\n\nconst play = {\n  pausable: true,\n  enter() { game.follow(hero, { z: 16 }); game.cam.bounds = v => map.bounds(v); game.lights.enabled = true; game.lights.ambient = .5; },\n  exit() { game.lights.enabled = false; ui.hud({}); },\n  update(dt) {\n    const I = game.input, was = !!(hero.wall || hero.action);\n    hero.update(dt, map, I);   // walks, jumps, climbs: the stick and the jump button, through the view\n    if (!was && (hero.wall || hero.action)) game.audio.sfx('jump');\n    // the guard walks the street and watches ahead: its eyes see over the planter, not through the roof\n    guard.vx = guard.dir * 30; guard.update(dt, map);\n    if (guard.x > 112 || guard.hitWall) guard.dir = -1; else if (guard.x < 40) guard.dir = 1;\n    guard.facing = guard.dir > 0 ? 0 : Math.PI;\n    const sees = map.sight(guard, hero) && E.inArc(guard, guard.facing, hero, 110, .6);\n    alert = sees ? alert + dt : Math.max(0, alert - dt * .5);\n    const gem = map.find('gem');\n    if (!got && E.dist(hero, { x: gem.x, y: gem.y, z: ROOF }) < 12) { got = true; game.audio.sfx('coin'); game.flash('#c8f4ff', .15); }\n    if (got && hero.z < 2) { won = true; game.go('end'); }   // back down in the street with it\n    else if (alert > 1.2) { won = false; game.audio.sfx('hurt'); game.go('end'); }\n    // the rigs are posed every step from the bodies' motion; draw only draws them\n    heroRig.update(dt, hero.rigState());\n    guardRig.update(dt, { x: guard.x, y: guard.y, z: guard.z, vx: guard.vx, vy: 0, facing: guard.facing, stance: 'ready' });\n    // the HUD, from this step's state (E.Shell redraws only what changed; the keys hide on a touch screen)\n    ui.hud({ objective: got ? { title: 'Bring it down', text: 'Back to the street with it' } : { title: 'Take the gem', text: hero.wall ? 'Climb: up, and jump to leap' : 'It lies on the roof', at: { x: gem.x, y: gem.y, z: ROOF }, from: hero },\n      bars: [{ label: 'Seen', value: Math.min(alert, 1.2), max: 1.2, color: '#ff6040' }, { label: 'Stamina', value: hero.stamina, max: hero.staminaMax, color: hero.exhausted ? '#ff6040' : '#7ad06a' }],\n      keys: [[['up', 'left', 'down', 'right'].map(a => I.label(a)).join(''), 'Move'], [I.label('jump'), 'Jump, climb, glide']] });\n  },\n  draw(r) {\n    map.drawFloor(r); map.queueWalls(r);   // (the floor runs on past the map to the screen's edges: map.outside)\n    for (const [id, x, y, o] of DRESS) r.shape(id, x, y, 0, o);\n    r.prop('lamp', 88, 88, 0, { light: true });   // a street lamp: its glow and a pool of light\n    r.decal(() => r.groundArc(guard.x, guard.y, 6, 110, guard.facing - .6, guard.facing + .6, alert > 0 ? '#ff6040' : '#ffe080', .4));   // its sight cone\n    const gem = map.find('gem');\n    if (!got) { r.sprite(gem.x, gem.y, ROOF + 6 + Math.sin(game.time * 3) * 2, GEM, { glow: .8 }); game.lights.add(gem.x, gem.y, ROOF + 6, 44, .9, { color: '#80d8ff' }); }\n    if (hero.gliding) r.queue(hero.x, hero.y, hero.z + 40, g => {   // the sail, over the hands the rig holds up\n      const c = Math.cos(hero.facing), s = Math.sin(hero.facing), P = (f, w, z) => r.w(hero.x + c * f - s * w, hero.y + s * f + c * w, hero.z + z);\n      const q = [P(9, -17, 43), P(9, 17, 43), P(-7, 15, 37), P(-7, -15, 37)], h = P(0, 0, 30);\n      for (const t of [q[0], q[1]]) E.px.line(g, t[0], t[1], h[0], h[1], '#3a2a20');\n      E.px.poly(g, q, '#d8603a'); E.px.line(g, q[0][0], q[0][1], q[1][0], q[1][1], '#f4a070');\n    });\n    for (const [b, rig] of [[hero, heroRig], [guard, guardRig]]) {\n      r.shadow(b.x, b.y, 7, .35, undefined, b.groundZ || 0);\n      r.actor(b.x, b.y, b.z, (g, ox, oy) => rig.draw(g, ox, oy, r.view));\n    }\n  }\n};\n\nconst end = {\n  update() { if (game.input.pressed('start')) { reset(); game.go('play'); } },\n  draw(r) {\n    r.sky(won ? ['#103020', '#2a6a48'] : ['#301010', '#6a2a2a']);\n    const m = Math.round(r.H / 2);\n    r.overlay(g => E.font.title(g, won ? 'STOLEN' : 'CAUGHT', r.W / 2, m - 42, { scale: 3, align: 'center' }));\n    r.text(('PRESS ' + game.input.label('start') + ' TO TRY AGAIN').toUpperCase(), r.W / 2, m + 28, '#ffffff', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000' });\n  }\n};\n\nreset();\n// a handle for tests and tools (node game/test.mjs, tools/check.mjs prints snapshot(), tools/replay.mjs logs it)\ngame.debug = {\n  snapshot: () => ({ scene: game.sceneName, hero: [hero.x, hero.y, hero.z].map(v => Math.round(v * 10) / 10), climbing: !!(hero.wall || hero.action),\n    guard: [Math.round(guard.x), Math.round(guard.y), guard.facing], alert: Math.round(alert * 100) / 100, got, won }),\n  teleport(x, y, z = 0, facing = hero.facing) { Object.assign(hero, { x, y, z, vx: 0, vy: 0, vz: 0, onGround: true, facing, wall: null, action: null }); }\n};\ngame.start({ scenes: { title, play, end }, scene: 'title' });\n})();","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium__20261102-192041__x694301/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01386X5GTeASzLX7cxZA7ivu","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
