o\n964:- `mover.dodge(dir, dist = 34)` †: a dodge roll toward dir (an angle or [dx, dy]; default its facing) when it stands free. Returns the action, or null\n965:- `mover.play(name, o = {})` †: start an action now (E.ACTIONS name, its options): it moves the body until it ends\n966:- `mover.respawn()` †: back to the last safe spot (after water, a pit, a fall it shouldn't survive)\n967:- `mover.rigState(extra)` †: the rig state: rig.update(dt, hero.rigState({ attack })): its motion, crouch, sprint and landing, or the playing action's pose; extra is merged over it\n968:- `mover.update(dt, map, ctl = {}, view)` †: one step. ctl: game.input (needs the actions move, jump, and sprint / crouch if it has them; screen directions turn into ground ones through view, the game's by default) or an intent { move: [dx, dy], sprint, crouch, jumpPressed }\n969:- `mover.accel = 700`, `mover.airAccel = 260` †: how fast it gets there\n970:- `mover.action = null` †: the E.Action playing, or null\n971:- `mover.buffer = .12` †: seconds a jump press is kept\n88:- 1161 21d. Shell; E.Shell: shell\n545:- `game.shell = null` †: the E.Shell over this game (an HTML interface: screens and HUD), or null\n627:- `saves.show(mode = 'load', done)` †: open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or a save. False without a menu (a headless game, menu: false)\n1163:- `new E.Shell(game, o = {}) → shell`: new E.Shell(game, { theme, screens: { name: spec }, settings: { items, onChange(settings, key) }, store: 'shell-settings', meters: .125, standard: true }): an HTML interface over the game (see the section's header)\n1164:- `new E.Shell({ theme })`: CSS variables (ink, paper, accent, muted, danger, line, font, titleFont)\n1165:- `new E.Shell({ screens })`: specs ui.show(name) starts from (the pause screen follows game.paused; screens: { pause: false } leaves it out)\n1166:- `new E.Shell({ settings })`: settings.items: the game's own settings,