{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0184aiMiczHgTtdeT13TFhXR","type":"tool_result","content":"5909:class FlowField {\nclass FlowField {\n  /**\n   * new E.FlowField(map, { step: 2, climb: 0, drop: 0, jump: 0 }): distances over the tops a body can stand on (E.HEIGHTS).\n   * With no options it covers the floor (and walls no higher than step, which bodies walk over); a target on a roof gets a\n   * field across the roofs it connects to\n   * - step, climb, drop: next-door cells connect when their tops differ by at most step, or going up by up to climb and\n   *   down by up to drop (agents that climb walls or hop down)\n   * - jump: (world units) links tops across a gap that a jump clears, straight along a row or column, by map.landing's\n   *   rules (up to jumpRise higher, 11, and jumpDrop lower, 18): an agent with E.Mover's leap chases across roofs. With\n   *   jump, distances are travel: a jump of k cells costs k, and a climb 1 plus its rise in cells (climbing is slow), so a\n   *   chase leaps a gap rather than drop into the street and climb back up\n   */\n  constructor(map, o = {}) {\n5988:  next(x, y) {\n6003:  dir(x, y, fx, fy) {\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium__20261102-192041__x694301/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1a5e6f5c-3967-4e9e-a458-94f8949fc080","uuid":"688a8e7d-e788-4289-98e5-43b9b679f528","timestamp":"2026-11-03T02:29:34.773Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"5909:class FlowField {\nclass FlowField {\n  /**\n   * new E.FlowField(map, { step: 2, climb: 0, drop: 0, jump: 0 }): distances over the tops a body can stand on (E.HEIGHTS).\n   * With no options it covers the floor (and walls no higher than step, which bodies walk over); a target on a roof gets a\n   * field across the roofs it connects to\n   * - step, climb, drop: next-door cells connect when their tops differ by at most step, or going up by up to climb and\n   *   down by up to drop (agents that climb walls or hop down)\n   * - jump: (world units) links tops across a gap that a jump clears, straight along a row or column, by map.landing's\n   *   rules (up to jumpRise higher, 11, and jumpDrop lower, 18): an agent with E.Mover's leap chases across roofs. With\n   *   jump, distances are travel: a jump of k cells costs k, and a climb 1 plus its rise in cells (climbing is slow), so a\n   *   chase leaps a gap rather than drop into the street and climb back up\n   */\n  constructor(map, o = {}) {\n5988:  next(x, y) {\n6003:  dir(x, y, fx, fy) {","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium__20261102-192041__x694301/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0184aiMiczHgTtdeT13TFhXR","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
